englishFull:
A case-inflected word compounds with river names to form अव्ययीभाव when the compound is a proper name (संज्ञा) denoting something other than the compound's literal meaning.

Since this forms a proper name, it is a नित्यसमास (invariable compound) — names cannot be expressed by uncompounded phrases.

@note[The संख्या from previous sūtras does not carry forward here.]
